.\" man/man5/docv-config.5
.TH DOCV\-CONFIG 5 2026-11-03 "docv 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
docv\-config \- configuration file of docv
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration of
.MR docv 1
is an INI file in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docv/config.ini ,
or
.I ~/.config/docv/config.ini
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or not an absolute path.
The first run writes it with every setting at its default, most of them
commented out.
.PP
A line
.BI [ section ]
starts a section; a line
.IB key " = " value
sets a key in it.
Lines starting with
.B ;
or
.B #
are comments; a comment cannot follow a value on the same line.
An unknown section or key, or an invalid value, is an error:
.B docv
reports it and exits with status 1.
.SH "THE [man] SECTION"
.TP
.B roff\-unsafe
Run the roff requests that execute commands or access files, and the
.B \eV
escape (environment variables).
Default
.BR false .
Booleans are
.BR true / false ,
.BR yes / no ,
.BR on / off
or
.BR 1 / 0 ,
in any case.
.RS
.PP
With
.BR true :
.B sy
and
.B pso
run commands with
.IR /bin/sh ,
.B pso
reading the output as input;
.B pi
pipes the page, formatted as text at 78 columns, into a command after
parsing;
.BR open ,
.BR opena ,
.BR write ,
.BR writec ,
.B writem
and
.B close
write files;
.B cf
and
.B trf
copy files into the page;
.B rd
reads input lines from the terminal, for the page named on the command line
only.
Commands run with standard input and output on the null device.
.PP
With
.B false
these requests are accepted and ignored.
Manual pages are input from third parties: enable this only if you trust
every page you open.
.RE
.TP
.B indent
The body indent of manual pages in the viewer, in columns (0 to 40).
Unset (the default), man(7) pages are indented 7 columns and mdoc(7) pages
5, as groff indents them.
.SH "THE [viewer] SECTION"
.TP
.B start\-wrapped
Start in the wrapped layout, paragraphs filled to the width of the
terminal.
With
.BR false ,
the viewer starts in the unwrapped layout: one line per paragraph, scrolled
sideways.
Default
.BR true .
.B w
switches between the layouts, and
.B \-u
on the command line starts unwrapped either way.
.TP
.B syntax\-highlighting
Color code examples by their syntax with tree-sitter grammars and their
.I highlights.scm
queries: Markdown code blocks labeled with a language, and the examples of
the pages
.B docv gen\-cr
makes.
Default
.BR true .
See
.B SYNTAX HIGHLIGHTING
in
.MR docv 1
for where grammars and queries are looked for.
.SH "THE [picker] SECTION"
The dock left of the page: its search field and tree of pages.
.TP
.B dock
Where the dock (search field and tree of pages, opened with
.BR p )
sits:
.B regular
narrows the page to make room for it,
.B overlay
covers the left of the page.
Default
.BR regular .
.TP
.B dock\-width
Width of the dock in columns, 16 to 400.
Dragging its right edge changes it until the viewer quits.
Default
.BR 36 .
.TP
.B dock\-open
Open the dock at start.
Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B min\-group
The fewest pages whose names share a prefix
.RB ( abrt\-cli ,
.BR abrt\-dump ", ...)"
that make a group in the tree, 2 to 1000.
Default
.BR 3 .
.TP
.B search\-threads
How many processes read the text of all pages, and how many threads search
it, for the hit counts of the tree while finding in the page (0 to 1024).
.B 0
is one less than the number of processors.
Default
.BR 0 .
.SH "THE [colors] SECTION"
Every element of the viewer is drawn in a role, and each key of this
section restyles one role.
A style is a list of words: attributes
.RB ( bold ,
.BR italic ,
.BR underline ,
.BR reverse ,
.BR dim ),
a foreground color, and
.B on
followed by a background color.
.PP
A color is
.BR default ,
.BR foreground ,
.BR background ,
one of the ANSI colors
.BR black ,
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR white ,
each also with a
.B bright\-
prefix, a palette number
.B 0
to
.BR 255 ,
or
.BI # rrggbb\c
\&.
Named and numbered colors are those of the terminal's theme.
A suffix
.BI + n
or
.BI \- n
ramps a color
.I n
percent toward the theme's foreground or background:
.B on background+12
is a background a shade off the terminal's in a dark and a light theme
alike, and
.B foreground\-40
is text dimmed toward the background.
.PP
With
.B NO_COLOR
set, colors are off and this section is ignored; the roles use attributes
only.
.PP
The roles and their defaults:
.TP
.B text
(plain) Plain page text.
.TP
.B heading1
.RB ( "bold bright\-blue" )
Section headings of manual pages, level 1 headings of documents.
.TP
.B heading2
.RB ( "bold blue" )
Subsection headings of manual pages, level 2 headings of documents.
.TP
.B heading3
.RB ( "bold bright\-magenta" )
Level 3 headings.
.TP
.B heading4
.RB ( "bold magenta" )
Level 4 headings.
.TP
.B heading5
.RB ( bold )
Level 5 headings.
.TP
.B heading6
.RB ( "bold foreground\-40" )
Level 6 headings.
.TP
.B bold
.RB ( "bold cyan" )
Bold page text: commands, options.
.TP
.B italic
.RB ( "underline green" )
Italic page text: arguments.
.TP
.B bold\-italic
.RB ( "bold underline green" )
Bold italic page text.
.TP
.B underline
.RB ( underline )
Underlined page text.
.TP
.B code
.RB ( "yellow on background+8" )
Inline code in documents.
.TP
.B code\-block
.RB ( yellow )
Code blocks in documents.
.TP
.B quote
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The bars of block quotes.
.TP
.B image
.RB ( "italic foreground\-40" )
The description standing for an image.
.TP
.B syntax\-keyword
.RB ( "bold magenta" )
Keywords in highlighted code.
.TP
.B syntax\-string
.RB ( green )
Strings and characters.
.TP
.B syntax\-comment
.RB ( "italic foreground\-45" )
Comments.
.TP
.B syntax\-function
.RB ( blue )
Functions, methods and constructors.
.TP
.B syntax\-type
.RB ( cyan )
Types, namespaces and modules.
.TP
.B syntax\-constant
.RB ( red )
Constants, numbers, booleans and built-in variables.
.TP
.B syntax\-operator
.RB ( foreground\-15 )
Operators.
.TP
.B syntax\-punctuation
.RB ( foreground\-35 )
Brackets and delimiters.
.TP
.B syntax\-property
.RB ( bright\-cyan )
Properties, fields and attributes.
.TP
.B syntax\-tag
.RB ( bright\-blue )
Markup tags.
.TP
.B link
.RB ( "underline magenta" )
Links: cross-references, files, headings, URLs.
.TP
.B link\-focus
.RB ( "reverse magenta" )
The focused link.
.TP
.B text\-selection
.RB ( "on blue\-50" )
Text selected with the mouse.
.TP
.B page\-header
.RB ( bold )
The page's heading in the title row; the source and date shown beside it
take
.BR detail .
.TP
.B title
.RB ( bold )
The title.
.TP
.B version
.RB ( foreground\-50 )
The version after the title.
.TP
.B close
.RB ( red )
The close mark.
.TP
.B border
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The line under the title row, the horizontal scrollbar track, the dock's
divider and the branches and lines of the dock's tree.
.TP
.B thumb
.RB ( "bold blue" )
Scrollbar thumbs.
.TP
.B rule
.RB ( foreground\-70 )
The rules under the page header and above the page footer, and horizontal
rules in documents.
.TP
.B field
.RB ( "on background+12" )
The search field; its ends take its background as their color.
.TP
.B prompt
.RB ( "bold blue" )
The leading
.B /
of a page search.
.TP
.B placeholder
.RB ( foreground\-50 )
The hint in the empty search field.
.TP
.B cursor
.RB ( reverse )
The cursor of the search field.
.TP
.B message
.RB ( yellow )
Messages in the status row.
.TP
.B status
.RB ( foreground\-30 )
The status row.
.TP
.B status\-separator
.RB ( foreground\-60 )
The separators between status parts.
.TP
.B name
.RB ( "bold cyan" )
Page names in the tree, and keys in the help.
.TP
.B document
.RB ( "bold magenta" )
Markdown document names in the tree.
.TP
.B detail
.RB ( foreground\-35 )
Page and document descriptions and the sections of page names in the tree.
.TP
.B button
.RB ( "bold blue" )
Group names in the tree.
.TP
.B button\-dim
.RB ( blue\-40 )
The
.B \[u25CB]
(open) and
.B \[u25CF]
(folded)
marks of groups in the tree.
.TP
.B tree\-guide
.RB ( background+15 )
The
.B \[u254E]
guides in the dock's tree, under a level that ended while an outer one
continues.
.TP
.B selection
.RB ( "on background+22" )
The selected row of the tree; the line of the selected match in the page.
.TP
.B hover
.RB ( "on background+10" )
The row of the tree under the pointer.
.TP
.B mark
.RB ( "bold underline yellow" )
Characters matched by a search.
.TP
.B hit
.RB ( "bold green" )
Pages in the dock's tree whose text has lines the search in the page
matches, and their counts.
.TP
.B popup
.RB ( "on background+6" )
The overlay dock.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
[man]
roff\-unsafe = false
indent = 4

[viewer]
start\-wrapped = false
syntax\-highlighting = false

[picker]
dock = overlay
dock\-width = 40
min\-group = 2

[colors]
heading1 = bold #ff8800
field = on background+8
selection = black on bright\-cyan
link = underline 208
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR docv 1
